############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML In our work so far, we've seen that raising the degree of polynomial improves the approximation of the original function [`f(x)\text{.}`] If we decided we wanted to find a degree [`9`] approximation to [`f(x) = \sin(x)\text{,}`] we'd need to find a polynomial whose value and first [`9`] derivatives match those of the sine function at [`x = 0\text{.}`]
