############################################################ # PG Setup Code ############################################################ $mc27 = CheckboxList([ ["${BM}S_n-S${EM} is going down in absolute value as ${BM}n${EM} increases.$BR", "${BM}S_n-S${EM} is going up in absolute value as ${BM}n${EM} increases.$BR", "${BM}S_n-S${EM} is going up and down in absolute value as ${BM}n${EM} increases.$BR", "${BM}S_n-S${EM} is negative when the partial sum is an underestimate.$BR", "${BM}S_n-S${EM} is positive when the partial sum is an underestimate.$BR", "${BM}S_n-S${EM} is negative when the partial sum is an overestimate.$BR", "${BM}S_n-S${EM} is positive when the partial sum is an overestimate.$BR", "${BM}S_n${EM} alternates back and forth between overestimates and underestimates.$BR", "${BM}S_n${EM} is always an overestimate.$BR", "${BM}S_n${EM} is always an underestimate.$BR" ]], [0,3,6,7] ); $mc = CheckboxList([ ["The absolute value of ${BM}S_n-S${EM} is always smaller than the absolute value of ${BM}a_n${EM}.$BR", "The absolute value of ${BM}S_n-S${EM} is sometimes smaller than the absolute value of ${BM}a_n${EM}.$BR", "The absolute value of ${BM}S_n-S${EM} is always larger than the absolute value of ${BM}a_n${EM}.$BR", "When ${BM}S_n-S${EM} is negative, ${BM}a_n${EM} is positive.$BR", "When ${BM}S_n-S${EM} is positive, ${BM}a_n${EM} is positive.$BR", "When ${BM}S_n-S${EM} is negative, ${BM}a_n${EM} is negative.$BR", "When ${BM}S_n-S${EM} is positive, ${BM}a_n${EM} is positive.$BR", "${BM}S_n+a_n = S_{n+1}${EM}.$BR", ]], [0,3,6,7] ); Context("LimitedNumeric");
############################################################ # Body ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML Consider the alternating geometric series
[``` S = \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} (-1)^k \left( \frac{4}{5} \right)^k = 1 - \frac{4}{5} + \frac{16}{25} - \cdots + (-1)^{n-1} \left( \frac{4}{5} \right)^{n-1} + \cdots \text{.}```]
We want to explore how the partial sums of the series compare to and approximate the exact sum of the series, which is
[```S = \frac{a}{1-r} = \frac{1}{1-\left(\frac{-4}{5}\right)} = \frac{1}{\frac{9}{5}} = \frac{5}{9}\text{.}```]
END_PGML
############################################################ # Scaffold ############################################################ Scaffold::Begin(numbered => 1,is_open => "correct_or_first_incorrect",can_open => always,);
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML Recall that the [`n`]th partial sum, [`S_n\text{,}`] is the sum of the first [`n`] terms of the infinite geometric series [`S\text{.}`] This means that
[``` S_n = \sum_{k=0}^{n-1} (-1)^k \left( \frac{4}{5} \right)^k = 1 - \frac{4}{5} + \frac{16}{25} - \cdots + (-1)^{n-1} \left( \frac{4}{5} \right)^{n-1} \text{.}```]
Note that the exact fractional values of [`S_1\text{,}`] [`S_2\text{,}`] [`\ldots\text{,}`] [`S_6\text{,}`] have been recorded below along with their decimal representations. Your task is to use this information to do some related computations that help us understand the behavior of the series and its partial sums.
First, by computing the differences between [`S_n`] and [`S`] for several different values of [`n`] (recalling that [`S = \frac{5}{9} = 0.\overline{5}`]), fill in the first column of blank spaces provided below. Then, by viewing the series
[```S = 1 - \frac{4}{5} + \frac{16}{25} - \cdots + (-1)^{n-1} \left( \frac{4}{5} \right)^{n-1} + \cdots```]
as being in the form
[```S = a_0 + a_1 + a_2 + \cdots\text{,}```]
fill in the last column of blank spaces.
[@KeyboardInstructions('Enter your answer in decimal form, using at least 4 digits after the decimal point if applicable.')@]**
>> [@DataTable( [ [PGML('[`n=1`]'), PGML('[`S_1=1`]'), PGML('[`S_1-S=`][_]{1-5/9}{10}'), PGML('[`a_1=-0.8`]'), ], [PGML('[`n=2`]'), PGML('[`S_2=\frac{1}{5}=0.2`]'), PGML('[`S_2-S=`][_]{0.2-5/9}{10}'), PGML('[`a_2=0.64`]'), ], [PGML('[`n=3`]'), PGML('[`S_3=\frac{21}{25}=0.84`]'), PGML('[`S_3-S=`][_]{0.84-5/9}{10}'), PGML('[`a_3=`][_]{-0.8**3}{10}'), ], [PGML('[`n=4`]'), PGML('[`S_4=\frac{41}{125}=0.328`]'), PGML('[`S_4-S=`][_]{0.328-5/9}{10}'), PGML('[`a_4=`][_]{0.8**4}{10}'), ], [PGML('[`n=5`]'), PGML('[`S_5=\frac{461}{625}=0.7376`]'), PGML('[`S_5-S=`][_]{0.7376-5/9}{10}'), PGML('[`a_5=`][_]{-0.8**5}{10}'), ], [PGML('[`n=6`]'), PGML('[`S_6=\frac{1281}{3125}=0.40992`]'), PGML('[`S_6-S=`][_]{0.40992-5/9}{10}'), PGML('[`a_6=`][_]{0.8**6}{10}'), ], ], align => '*{4}{l}', valign => 'middle',);@]* <<
END_PGML
